WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.629 align:start position:0%
 
the house select committee investigating  the capital riot wrapped its first  series of public hearings on thursday we  have far more evidence to share with the  american people and more to gather the  committee was formed in the wake of the  january 6 20  attack on the capitol  in order to find out what happened the  eight televised hearings aimed to make  the case that former president donald  trump was accountable for the attack and  that it was the result of a  multi-pronged conspiracy trump has said  he's done nothing wrong and has called  the committee a partisan witch-hunt  the journal scott patterson explains how  the committee has presented evidence  they say shows that trump failed to  intervene after setting the stage for  the riot promoted baseless accusations  of election fraud and led a pressure  campaign to overturn the 2020 election  the committee's latest primetime session  zeroed in on trump's activities inside  the white house during the 187 minutes  after he gave his speech at the ellipse  on january 6.  according to live and recorded testimony  on thursday trump spent more than two  and a half hours in front of a  television in his private dining room as  rioters breached the capitol what people  were really asking president trump to do  including his own family and top  officials in the white house was for him  to put out a statement to the rioters to  stop and leave the capitol building  if the president had wanted to make a  statement  and address the american people he could  have been on camera almost instantly the  committee also played outtakes from a  video recorded at the white house on  january 7 2021 which showed that the  former president still refused to  concede that he lost the election this  election is now over  congress has certified the results i  don't want to say the election is over i  just want to say  congress has certified the results  without saying the election's over okay  it was the first time in history united  states that we did not have  a peaceful transfer of power  [Music]  cassidy hutchinson a one-time aide to  white house chief of staff mark meadows  testified in an earlier hearing that  trump knew that his supporters were  armed when he urged them to march to the  capitol  hutchinson said trump is briefed about  the presence of weapons at the rally but  was concerned that magnetometers were  keeping supporters from attending  i overheard the president say something  to the effect of you know i don't even  care that they have weapons  they're not here to hurt me take the  effing bags away  despite knowing all this he stands  before them and says  go to the capitol  the committee played never-before-seen  footage of rioters breaching the  building as officers braced for the  assault  testimony from capitol police officer  caroline edwards described the attacks  as a war scene i saw friends with blood  all over their faces i was slipping in  people's blood  the goal of that was to really show to  the american public many of whom may not  have seen footage like this before how  violent it was steven ayers a former  trump supporter who pleaded guilty to  breaching the capital testified that he  initially had no intention of going  there on the sixth basically  you know the president  you know got everybody riled up  told everybody head on down  so we basically just following what he  said  video showed rioters reading a tweet  sent by trump that criticized then vice  president mike pence for refusing to  block the electoral college count my  our kids and our constitution  the committee detailed the potential  peril to pence who became a clear target  of the mob  [Applause]  the crowds surged and within one minute  of trump's tweet made it to one floor  below where pence was waiting off the  senate floor  vice president pence and his team  ultimately were led to a secure location  where they stayed for the next four and  a half hours  barely missing rioters a few feet away  the main point that the committee was  trying to make with this is how trump  has this power over his followers and  they do what he says and he knows that  according to videotaped depositions  trump is told repeatedly by top justice  department officials and members of his  inner circle that he hadn't won the 2020  election and that claims a voter fraud  were without merit i told him that it  was  it was  crazy stuff trump continued to spread  election fraud claims including ones  that election workers brought a suitcase  full of fake ballots into an atlanta  voting facility evidence of fraud is  overwhelming and again i'm going to ask  you to look up at that very very  powerful and very expensive screen  hidden cases of possible ballots are  rolled out from under a table four  people under a cloud of suspicion  gabriel sterling a top republican  georgia election official addressed the  claims and testimony to the committee  what it actually showed was fulton  county election workers engaging in  normal ballot processing testimony from  georgia's secretary of state brad  raffensberger detailed requests by trump  aimed at overturning the election  results look all i want to do is this i  just want to find  uh  11  780  votes which is one more that we have  because we won the state there were no  votes to find that was an accurate count  that had been certified ruby freeman who  was a georgia election worker also  testified about how she received threats  so severe that at one point she went  into hiding after trump accused her of  participating in voter fraud  there is nowhere i feel safe  nowhere  do you know how it feels to have  the president of the united states to  target you  the public hearings laid out the  committee's view of the attack on the  capitol as a watershed historical moment  for american democracy and a red alarm  for threats it could face in the future  what they're saying is that they  continue to hear from new witnesses we  don't know who these people are but  we're being told that there's enough to  merit further hearings members of the  january 6 committee have indicated they  believe trump broke the law when he  attempted to overturn the 2020  presidential election but they have no  power to initiate a criminal  investigation they can't make charges  that's not their role but it is the role  of the doj the justice department is  conducting its own parallel  investigation into the january 6 attack  we are seeing signs that the  investigation is widening and  potentially looking at individuals in  trump's inner circle although as of yet  we don't have any sign that the doj is  is looking at mr trump himself  [Music]

